## Tasks

### 1. Add commit_sha to EventMetadata
- Add `commit_sha: Option<String>` to EventMetadata
- Populate it in git.rs `get_all_events()` from `commit.id().to_string()`
- Unit test: event metadata from git store includes sha

### 2. Add format_narrative() to EventFormat trait
- Add `fn format_narrative(&self, author: &str) -> String` to EventFormat
- Compiler will force implementation on all event types
- Implement for each:
  - AddedEvent: "author added name" / "author added name under parent"
  - RemovedEvent: "author removed id"
  - MovedEvent: "author moved id under parent" / "author moved id to root"
  - FieldUpdatedEvent: smart formatting based on field_name
    (.state → started/finished/reset, .context.md → updated context,
     .tags → tagged with, name → renamed, other → updated field on)
- Add format_narrative() on YakEvent, delegating to inner types.
  Compacted → "author compacted the event stream (N yaks)"
- Unit tests for each event type's narrative

### 3. Add relative timestamp formatting
- Add chrono-humanize dependency (or similar)
- Create helper fn: if ≤7 days → humanized relative, else → absolute
- Unit test the 7-day cutoff

### 4. Rewrite log_entry display
- Update UserDisplay::log_entry signature to accept structured data
  (narrative, relative_time, event_id, commit_sha)
- Implement 3-line format:
  Line 1: narrative (bold yak names when color enabled)
  Line 2: timestamp (dim)
  Line 3: event: id  sha: short_sha (dim)
  Then: ──────── rule
- Handle no-color: same lines without ANSI codes

### 5. Update show_log use case
- Wire up: build narrative from event, format timestamp, pass sha
- Compacted: single summary line instead of expanded snapshots

### 6. Update acceptance tests
